Article 7
The Community has obligations and responsibilities toward the Protection of Women and Children through Community participation activities in the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children in the form of: providing information and/or reporting every occurrence of vulnerability risk and Violence that comes to their knowledge;
facilitating deliberation to reach consensus for the creation of restorative justice for Children in conflict with the law through informal channels and implemented at the village/kelurahan government level and institutional authorities;
identifying/early detection and initial handling of Children at risk;
mediation and guidance for families experiencing Violence in the household, household conflicts, and divorce;
preparation of families and the Community in receiving Children who are victims of maltreatment and/or Children at risk; and the process of repatriation, social Rehabilitation, and social Reintegration.

Article 10
Every Woman has the right to:
a. 	live, sustain life and improve her standard of living;
b. 	live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously both physically and spiritually;
c. 	enjoy a good and healthy living environment;
d. 	live in a family within the bonds of lawful marriage based on the provisions of laws and regulations;
e. 	obtain work in accordance with her abilities, appropriate conditions and fair and just wages;
f. 	specifically for Women with disabilities, the right to obtain facilities and special treatment in public services;
g. 	play an active role in the field of politics and government in accordance with the potential and capabilities she possesses;
h. 	obtain legal information and services;
i. 	obtain services to increase her income; and
j. 	obtain other rights in accordance with her human dignity and based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

